<.page site_key={@site_key} title="Acme — Docs" active="docs">
  <h1>Documentation</h1>
  <p>A long page, useful for comparing scroll depth against the shorter ones.</p>

  <div :for={n <- 1..12} class="filler">
    <h2>Chapter {n}</h2>
    <p>
      Dwell time on this page accrues every second while the tab is visible and the
      visitor has interacted recently. Switch to another tab and the seconds keep
      counting as dwell but stop counting as active — which is exactly the gap the
      idle-tab anomaly rule looks for.
    </p>
    <a href={"#chapter-#{n}"} class="btn">Anchor link {n}</a>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <a href={~p"/demo"} class="btn">Back to home</a>
    <a href={~p"/demo/pricing"} class="btn btn-primary">See pricing</a>
  </div>
</.page>
